config CRUX_FILE_FATFS_RT1060
    bool "Crux File FatFs provider on the RT1060-EVKB microSD"
    depends on CRUX_PILOT_MODULE && BOARD_MIMXRT1060_EVK && SOC_MIMXRT1062
    depends on BOARD_MIMXRT1060_EVK_MIMXRT1062_QSPI && BOARD_REVISION_B
    depends on FAT_FILESYSTEM_ELM && FILE_SYSTEM && DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC
    depends on DT_HAS_NXP_IMX_USDHC_ENABLED && DT_HAS_ZEPHYR_SDMMC_DISK_ENABLED
    depends on FS_FATFS_LFN && FS_FATFS_MAX_LFN >= 127 && FS_FATFS_REENTRANT
    depends on !FS_FATFS_MOUNT_MKFS
    help
      Link the File provider into an RT1060-EVKB image. Off by default. It mounts and
      formats nothing by itself; the project composition owns mount order and recovery.
      Physical-board evidence is narrow: runs of earlier revisions (2 and 3 November 2026) on
      one RT1060-EVKB and one microSD card (docs/evidence/microsd-physical,
      microsd-power-cut and microsd-card-states-stack), with plain crux_file appends and
      reads. The replace-and-rename power-cut loop (microsd-replace-cut) called Zephyr
      fs_rename directly, and the card-states-stack probe ran create, rename, stat, list and
      remove through Zephyr fs_* directly (sample sd_probe.c), not crux_file. It qualifies neither the board, the card nor the
      Settings File backend. The roots, stat, size, rename and listing operations that
      crux_file gained later (#224) have no physical run.

config CRUX_FILE_FATFS_RT1060_RAM_DISK
    bool "Crux File FatFs provider on a RAM disk of the RT1060-EVKB"
    depends on CRUX_PILOT_MODULE && BOARD_MIMXRT1060_EVK && SOC_MIMXRT1062
    depends on BOARD_MIMXRT1060_EVK_MIMXRT1062_QSPI && BOARD_REVISION_B
    depends on FAT_FILESYSTEM_ELM && FILE_SYSTEM && DISK_DRIVER_RAM
    depends on !DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC && !DISK_DRIVER_FLASH
    depends on FS_FATFS_LFN && FS_FATFS_MAX_LFN >= 127 && FS_FATFS_REENTRANT
    depends on !FS_FATFS_MOUNT_MKFS
    help
      Link the File provider into an RT1060-EVKB image whose only disk is a RAM disk, so that no
      card can be reached by it and nothing persists across a reset. Off by default. It needs the
      SD card driver to be absent: a build that has both is refused here and by the provider's
      CMake. It mounts and formats nothing by itself; the composition owns the mount, and may
      format a RAM disk because it is memory. Used by the bench image of the integrated
      management composition (tests/zephyr/management_rt1060_compile, which declares it).
      No physical-board result exists for this selection.

